// The café's coffee survey – a sibling of cafe.json5 for the one lesson the café's own items cannot
// teach: an unfolding (ideal-point) item, used by the Unfolding block of
// docs/en/concepts/latent-variables.md. The café asked 200 loyalty members how far they agree with
// six statements about the coffee they like, each describing a strength from milky to black. A
// member agrees with the statements near their own taste and disagrees with those too mild or too
// strong for them, so agreement peaks where the member's taste meets the statement's – it does not
// rise steadily with the trait, as a satisfaction item's does. Generated by the exam builder's
// authored spec format (docs/en/exam-spec-reference.md):
//
//   app-gen --spec docs/examples/cafe-coffee.json5 --name cafe-coffee --authored
//
// The name is the seed, so `--name cafe-coffee` reproduces the dataset exactly; cafe-coffee.csv is
// that dataset, written as cafe.csv is. Every number the concept page quotes from it comes from
// that file, so a change to anything here – the name included – is a change to the prose.
// cafe-coffee.ru.csv is this dataset with its header translated, every value identical – the Russian
// docs quote it, so a change here is a change to both files.
//
// Structure: one trait, Strength – how strong a member likes their coffee, mean 0 and SD 1 across
// the members. Each statement is a GGUM item, answered 1 = strongly disagree … 4 = strongly agree,
// with the same discrimination (1.5) and latitudes (1.6, 1.1, 0.5, as the IRT table prints them) and
// its ideal point spaced evenly from −1.5 (the mildest) to 1.5 (the strongest), so a GGUM fit in the
// IRT module can be read against the planted positions. No missing data and no deliberate flaws.
{
	n: 200,
	factors: ["Strength"],
	variables: {
		// "I like milky drinks where the coffee is barely there"
		milky: { factor: "Strength", family: "ggum", params: [1.5, -1.5, 1.6, 1.1, 0.5] },
		// "A latte is about as strong as I like it"
		latte: { factor: "Strength", family: "ggum", params: [1.5, -0.9, 1.6, 1.1, 0.5] },
		// "A regular filter coffee suits me"
		filter: { factor: "Strength", family: "ggum", params: [1.5, -0.3, 1.6, 1.1, 0.5] },
		// "I like a flat white – more coffee than milk"
		flatwhite: { factor: "Strength", family: "ggum", params: [1.5, 0.3, 1.6, 1.1, 0.5] },
		// "A straight espresso is my kind of coffee"
		espresso: { factor: "Strength", family: "ggum", params: [1.5, 0.9, 1.6, 1.1, 0.5] },
		// "I want my coffee as strong and black as it comes"
		black: { factor: "Strength", family: "ggum", params: [1.5, 1.5, 1.6, 1.1, 0.5] },
	},
}
